articles.content_en:
Article 1 The arbitration judicial review cases as referred to in these Provisions include the following cases:
(1) Cases applying for confirmation of the validity of an arbitration agreement;
(2) Cases applying for enforcement of an arbitral award made by an arbitration institution in the mainland of China;
(3) Cases applying for setting aside an arbitral award made by an arbitration institution in the mainland of China;
(4) Cases applying for recognition and enforcement of an arbitral award made in the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, the Macao Special Administrative Region, or the Taiwan Region;
(5) Cases applying for recognition and enforcement of a foreign arbitral award;
(6) Other arbitration judicial review cases.

Article 5 Where an applicant applies to a People's Court for confirmation of the validity of an arbitration agreement, it shall submit a written application and the original copy of the arbitration agreement or a certified true copy thereof.
The written application shall state the following:
(1) Where the applicant or the respondent is a natural person, the application shall state its/his/her name, sex, date of birth, nationality, and domicile; where it is a legal person or any other organization, the application shall state its name and domicile and the name and position of its legal representative or representative;
(2) The content of the arbitration agreement;
(3) The specific request and the reasons therefor.
Any application, arbitration agreement, or other document in a foreign language submitted by a party shall be accompanied by a Chinese translation.

Article 6 Where an applicant applies to a People's Court for enforcement or setting aside of an arbitral award made by an arbitration institution in the mainland of China, or applies for recognition and enforcement of a foreign arbitral award, it shall submit a written application and the original copy of the arbitral award or a certified true copy thereof.
The written application shall state the following:
(1) Where the applicant or the respondent is a natural person, the application shall state its/his/her name, sex, date of birth, nationality, and domicile; where it is a legal person or any other organization, the application shall state its name and domicile and the name and position of its legal representative or representative;
(2) The main content of the arbitral award and the date on which it takes effect;
(3) The specific request and the reasons therefor.
Any application, arbitral award, or other document in a foreign language submitted by a party shall be accompanied by a Chinese translation.
